= The purpose of this note

After reading several books and a lot of YouTube videos on mathematical finance in general, I couldn't find a concise summary of the problem at hand in a very concrete manner. The introductions often include a brief recap of history, then define the asset classes and simple metrics for a couple of chapters, and only after that the fun begins.

I found myself pretty lost in where we are heading from time to time, or worst, found myself ended up not learning something very meaningful after reading five chapters. I personally prefers books that give me the big picture of the topics before diving into the detail, and this is why I want to make this Atlas for mathematical finance, mostly for myself.
